        ":question/id": "b300142b-b3f8-5894-8187-0c36b823a692",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5 e^{4}}^{5 e^{9}}\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\ln \\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5 e^{4}$ | $5 e^{9}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $9$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5 e^{4}}^{5 e^{9}}\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\ln(\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right))}}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{25}\\int_{5 e^{4}}^{5 e^{9}}\\sqrt{\\ln(\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right))}\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int_{4}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int_{4}^{9}u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot\\frac{u^{3/2}}{3/2}\\right)|_{4}^{9} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(u^{3/2}\\right)|_{4}^{9} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(9^{3/2}-4^{3/2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(27-8\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(19\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
